  "question": "Description of the required functions of a credit card management system:\n1. Credit card application:\nNon-credit card customers fill out the credit card application form, and the system records the application number, customer number (the customer number can be temporarily empty at this time, and will be associated after the application is successful), the type of credit card applied for, the name of the applicant, the ID number of the applicant, the time of application submission, and the application result (initially set to \"pending review\").\nThe bank reviews the application. If the application is accepted, it generates a unique customer number, records the customer name, credit card type (i.e. the type of credit card applied for), generates a credit card number, sets the validity period and credit limit, and records the creation time and update time. At the same time, the customer number and application result of the corresponding application record in the \"Credit Card Application\" table are updated to \"approved\". The system sends a confirmation letter to the customer; if the application is not approved, the application result in the \"Credit Card Application\" table is updated to \"rejected\", and a rejection letter is sent to the customer.\n3. Transaction information query:\nFor each transaction made by a credit card customer using a credit card, the system will generate a unique transaction number, record the customer number, transaction time, transaction amount, transaction type, and transaction description.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0468\nCREATE TABLE `credit_card_application` (\n  `application_no` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer_no` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `card_type` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `applicant_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `applicant_id_no` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `submission_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `application_result` varchar(20) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending review',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`application_no`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `credit_card_customer` (\n  `customer_no` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `application_no` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `card_type` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `credit_card_no` varchar(32) NOT NULL,\n  `valid_from` date NOT NULL,\n  `valid_to` date NOT NULL,\n  `credit_limit` decimal(12,2) NOT NULL,\n  `created_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_no`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `uk_credit_card_customer_credit_card_no` (`credit_card_no`),\n  KEY `credit_card_customer_ibfk_1` (`application_no`),\n  CONSTRAINT `credit_card_customer_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`application_no`) REFERENCES `credit_card_application` (`application_no`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `credit_card_transaction` (\n  `transaction_no` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer_no` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_amount` decimal(12,2) NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`transaction_no`),\n  KEY `credit_card_transaction_ibfk_1` (`customer_no`),\n  CONSTRAINT `credit_card_transaction_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_no`) REFERENCES `credit_card_customer` (`customer_no`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
